WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:03.030
Harry Kersh: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.530
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:07.690
between Domino's pizza
in the UK and the US.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.236
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:13.483 --> 00:00:15.930
This is the smallest pizza
you can get in the UK.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:17.220
It's called an individual,

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.220
and it measures 7 inches across.

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.860
Joe Avella: Our smallest is,
believe it or not, this small.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:26.460
Here it is, and it measures
in diameter 10 inches.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.930
Harry: The next size up is a small,

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:30.613
which measures 9.5 inches.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:33.644
Joe: Next size up for
the US is our medium,

00:00:33.644 --> 00:00:36.302
which is 12 inches.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:41.258
Harry: This is 11.5 inches.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.776
Joe: What? I'm starving.

00:00:45.965 --> 00:00:48.993
Hey, I grabbed a slice.

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:51.690
I'm starving. This pizza smells so good.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:52.707
I skipped breakfast.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:55.679
Next pizza.

00:00:55.679 --> 00:00:57.337
Next up for the US is our large,

00:00:57.337 --> 00:01:00.070
which is a 14-inch diameter.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:01.085
Oh, hell, yeah.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:07.413
What's with the way they
cut your large pizza, Harry?

00:01:07.413 --> 00:01:09.750
It's ridiculous. Look at that.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.260
And not to be outdone,

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:14.500
the US has one more size, the extra large.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.480
Diameter, 16 inches. Bro!

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.030
Look at the size of this thing.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.148
Harry: Now, a 2.5-inch difference

00:01:23.148 --> 00:01:24.531
might not sound like a lot,

00:01:24.531 --> 00:01:26.480
but if you factor that
into the surface area,

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:29.121
it's actually 58 square inches wider

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:30.896
than the UK's largest pizza,

00:01:30.896 --> 00:01:32.881
which is almost a third of an increase.

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:35.040
Joe: Am I looking at this right?

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.370
Is it supposed to be six slices?

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.380
It's six slices. That can't be right.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:41.515
Six slices for a extra-large pizza?

00:01:41.515 --> 00:01:43.190
Look at the size of these slices!

00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:47.610
In the US at a Domino's,

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:49.401
the extra-large pizza will cost you

00:01:49.401 --> 00:01:51.692
a very reasonable $13.99.

00:01:52.794 --> 00:01:53.727
Hm.

00:01:55.342 --> 00:01:57.002
That...circle....

00:01:57.002 --> 00:02:01.810
That is 201 square inches,

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:03.867
which breaks down to roughly

00:02:03.867 --> 00:02:05.767
7 cents an inch?

00:02:05.767 --> 00:02:07.120
Nice.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.450
Harry: Now, shockingly,
$13.99 will only get you

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.590
a small pizza in the UK.

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:14.350
A small pizza is 9.5 inches across,

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:17.790
and that gives it a surface
area of 71 square inches.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:21.787
Now, if you divide the
$13.69 price tag by the 71,

00:02:21.787 --> 00:02:23.051
you find out that you're actually paying

00:02:23.051 --> 00:02:25.810
19 cents per square inch.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.660
Ultimately, it means that
if you went into a US

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:30.410
and a UK Domino's with $13.99 to spend,

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.420
you'd be able to get more
than double the pizza

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.185
for your money in the US store.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.950
Let's compare large cheese
pizzas in the two countries.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:45.450
This is what a UK large cheese looks like.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.460
Joe: And this is what a large,

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:51.360
properly cut Domino's cheese
pizza looks like in the US.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.080
Harry: It's cut into 10 pieces,

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:56.700
and each slice contains 176 calories.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.020
That means that in total,

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:02.210
the pizza in the UK is 1,760 calories.

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:04.160
Joe: Instead of 10, we got eight slices.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:07.410
That means each slice
is roughly 280 calories,

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:11.800
which makes the whole
pizza 2,240 calories.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.920
And according to the thing
that was written for me,

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:18.000
that is almost 480 calories
more than the UK large.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.490
Harry: But why is that exactly?

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.741
Let's see if we can get any
clues from the ingredients.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:26.890
Let's start with the
foundation of any pizza,

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.080
which is the dough.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:31.260
In the UK, the dough
is made of wheat flour,

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:35.770
a wheat and milk premix,
rapeseed oil, water, and yeast.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:37.262
Joe: Yes, but here in the US,

00:03:37.262 --> 00:03:39.936
our dough is made of...

00:03:39.936 --> 00:03:41.228
enriched flour, wheat -

00:03:41.228 --> 00:03:42.700
oh, God, I hate reading this stuff.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:45.060
Enriched flour, which
is wheat flour, iron,

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:48.430
thiamine mononitrate, niacin, riboflavin,

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:51.130
and folic acid, water, soybean oil.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.183
And it contains less
than 2% of the following:

00:03:53.183 --> 00:03:54.949
sugar, salt, whey,

00:03:54.949 --> 00:03:57.752
maltodextrin, dextrose,

00:03:57.752 --> 00:04:02.610
dough conditioners such as
sodium stearoyl lacksi...

00:04:03.632 --> 00:04:04.598
lactylate.

00:04:04.598 --> 00:04:05.814
I don't know. It's on the screen.

00:04:05.814 --> 00:04:07.089
You read it out loud.

00:04:07.089 --> 00:04:09.914
Enzymes! Calcium sulfate,

00:04:09.914 --> 00:04:11.850
ascorbic acid, calcium phosphate,

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.060
L-cysteine. Good for hangovers, I hear.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.910
Yeast and cornmeal.

00:04:17.571 --> 00:04:19.150
Uh, yeah, much different.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:20.866
A lot more chemicals.

00:04:20.866 --> 00:04:23.070
Who saw that coming? [laughs]

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:24.340
Harry: How about the cheese?

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.093
Domino's in the UK refers to its cheese

00:04:26.093 --> 00:04:28.390
simply as mozzarella, and it's mostly

00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:30.980
because the ingredients are just that.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:34.210
Joe: In the US, Domino's
doesn't - possibly can't -

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:35.690
call their cheese mozzarella.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:39.240
Instead, they refer to
it as "pizza cheese."

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:42.650
So, the Domino's in
the US's "pizza cheese"

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.840
has the following ingredients.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.259
Part-skim mozzarella cheese, OK,

00:04:47.259 --> 00:04:48.610
which is pasteurized milk,

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:50.550
cultures, salt, enzymes,

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:55.500
modified food starch,
cellulose, nonfat milk,

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.880
whey protein concentrate, natural flavors,

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.921
and sodium proponiate.

00:05:00.921 --> 00:05:03.637
Prop-io-nate.

00:05:03.637 --> 00:05:04.612
Propionate.

00:05:04.612 --> 00:05:06.430
Harry: Now let's look at the pepperoni.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:08.640
Most of the ingredients
in US and UK pepperoni

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:10.180
are actually pretty similar.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.640
They both contain pork, salt, dextrose,

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.672
spices, sodium nitrite, citric acid,

00:05:16.672 --> 00:05:19.160
flavorings, and starter culture.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.480
Joe: You know, the only difference is

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.040
that our pepperoni contains beef.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:27.260
Also preservatives
beutohydrolate, hydrolazinase,

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.460
and beautohadalid blabbity blah.

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:31.220
BHA and BHT.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:34.560
I can't pronounce them.
They're bad. [laughs]

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.950
Harry: It turns out BHA
and BHT are actually

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:39.120
subject to restrictions
in the European Union

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.770
and can't be added to
foods such as pepperoni.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:43.261
This might be because studies have shown

00:05:43.261 --> 00:05:45.740
that BHA can cause tumors in rats

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.800
and is therefore reasonably anticipated

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.885
to be a carcinogen in humans.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:55.687
Joe: Oh, well.

00:05:57.728 --> 00:05:59.545
I'm gonna die doing what I love.

00:06:00.522 --> 00:06:03.820
Eating banned chemicals. Mm!

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:05.600
Harry: We reached out to
Domino's to get some clarity

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:07.320
on the pepperoni situation.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:09.700
We got our info from
their ingredients webpage.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:10.830
However, when we checked with them,

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:12.950
they told us that their
information was incorrect,

00:06:12.950 --> 00:06:15.010
and they've updated it
since to say that BHA

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:17.820
and BHT have now been
removed from the pepperoni.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:20.350
I think this happened at
some point during 2018.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:21.713
They couldn't say exactly when.

00:06:21.713 --> 00:06:23.557
But, Joe, it sounds like
you're OK after all.

00:06:31.759 --> 00:06:33.157
Here are all the items you can only find

00:06:33.157 --> 00:06:35.400
on the menu at a UK Domino's.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.730
Joe: And here are all the
things you can only get

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.340
at a US Domino's.

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.730
Harry: Let's start with the pizza itself.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:43.920
So, firstly is the crust options.

00:06:43.920 --> 00:06:46.130
Now, in the UK, we can
actually get stuffed crust.

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:49.180
But what we've gone for here
is the Italian-style crust.

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:51.390
Apologies to the country
of Italy for this one.

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:54.470
Now, the Italian crust is
basically the same dough

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:57.620
but just thinner and
therefore a bit more crispy.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:06:59.180
There are a few toppings
that you can only get

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:00.740
on your pizza in the UK.

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:02.290
These include some options we've got here,

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:06.180
like meatballs, sweet corn, and red onion.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:07.020
But that's not all.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:09.220
You can also get things
like Catalan chicken,

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:11.910
which is a chicken in a
kind of paprika spice.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.340
You can get tandoori chicken,

00:07:13.340 --> 00:07:15.860
which is chicken with
some Indian spice blends.

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:18.150
And you can also get tuna on your pizza.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:18.983
Joe: Whoa, wait.

00:07:18.983 --> 00:07:22.120
Did he say tuna? Tuna on a pizza?

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:23.910
No, no way.

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:26.142
So, this right here is a pizza that has

00:07:26.142 --> 00:07:28.360
everything you can only
get at a US Domino's.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:29.750
First of all, the crust.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:32.380
It is our thin Brooklyn-style crust.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:35.570
Instead of tomato sauce, we
did an Alfredo white sauce.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:37.230
We got banana peppers on here,

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:42.230
salami, feta cheese, and
also Parmesan and cheddar.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.250
This should be known as The US Only.

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:46.990
Like, Pizza Hut should
have this on the menu,

00:07:46.990 --> 00:07:48.513
and you go, "Give me The US Only."

00:07:48.513 --> 00:07:49.688
And this is the pizza they give you.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:57.386
Yuck. Don't get this.

00:07:57.386 --> 00:07:59.311
[laughing]

00:08:01.112 --> 00:08:02.296
Yeah, I hate that.

00:08:04.061 --> 00:08:05.320
Grab a slice. See what you think.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:06.560
Harry: So, here are some UK sides

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:09.070
that you won't find on
the menu at a US Domino's.

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:11.470
First of all, we've got
the garlic cheesy bread.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:13.520
Chicken Kickers, which are just, like,

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:15.530
nuggets with a spicy coating.

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:17.121
Pretty recently, they've added these

00:08:17.121 --> 00:08:18.854
Pop'n Chicken bites to the menu,

00:08:18.854 --> 00:08:22.260
which, kind of similar
to KFC's popcorn chicken.

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:23.920
You can also get Chicken Strippers,

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:25.650
which is just kind of
like chicken tenders.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:27.008
Potato wedges, if you wanted

00:08:27.008 --> 00:08:29.512
some kind of potato option
to go with your pizza,

00:08:29.512 --> 00:08:33.020
and then you can also
get a tub of coleslaw.

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:34.790
Joe: I don't think we
have garlic cheesy bread,

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:38.490
but we do have this, which is
like a stuffed cheese bread.

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:41.570
Also, this side, they
have these chicken pieces,

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:43.410
and then, these right over here,

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:47.667
these Parmesan cheese kind of bread knots.

00:08:47.667 --> 00:08:48.930
[crunching]

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:50.758
Also I think it's pretty
cool, is Domino's will

00:08:50.758 --> 00:08:52.870
hook you up with a side
of grated Parmesan.

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:54.000
That's pretty nice.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:56.788
Chicken carbonara, which is a pasta dish,

00:08:56.788 --> 00:08:59.355
but looks like obviously chicken,

00:08:59.355 --> 00:09:01.260
bits of bacon, onion.

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:03.908
In the US, Domino's
offers a lot of different

00:09:03.908 --> 00:09:06.320
varieties of sandwiches.
I just picked one.

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:07.910
I got the chicken Parm sandwich.

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:09.730
Let's take a look at that right there.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:11.450
Look at that chicken Parm.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.890
How good does that look?

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:14.490
Classic garden salad.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.851
We found something green
on the menu, which is nice.

00:09:18.127 --> 00:09:19.943
What do we got here? Tomatoes, onions,

00:09:19.943 --> 00:09:23.257
cheese, lettuce, croutons.

00:09:23.257 --> 00:09:25.650
[sighs] Who cares?

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:27.220
Harry: Now, the default
dipping sauce that will come

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:30.281
with your pizzas is this
garlic and herb dip in the UK.

00:09:30.281 --> 00:09:31.610
But there are also a couple of sauces

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:33.870
which are exclusive to the UK.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:37.097
These include a little pot
of Frank's RedHot sauce,

00:09:37.097 --> 00:09:39.573
and we can also get a honey mustard.

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:43.590
Joe: The Domino's in the US
has their own exclusive sauces.

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:48.420
This kicker hot sauce, the
sweet mango habanero sauce.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:49.763
This one is really good.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:52.546
Ranch. You guys don't have ranch?

00:09:52.546 --> 00:09:54.071
Thought you did. Guess not.

00:09:54.071 --> 00:09:56.271
Blue cheese dressing, mm.

00:09:56.271 --> 00:09:58.700
And, of course, marinara sauce.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.930
Harry: And finally, if you're
someone with a sweet tooth,

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:03.880
Domino's has some exclusive
dessert items in the UK.

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:05.530
Firstly, we've got Domino's cookies,

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:07.140
which are actually, like, really good,

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.040
especially if you get
them when they're warm,

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.206
and they kind of stay warm

00:10:10.206 --> 00:10:12.090
when they rest on the pizza boxes.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.865
And then you can also get a range

00:10:13.865 --> 00:10:16.306
of Ben and Jerry's flavors
from Domino's in the UK.

00:10:16.306 --> 00:10:18.400
They're, like, a licensed
vendor, which is cool.

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:19.562
Joe: And for dessert in the US,

00:10:19.562 --> 00:10:22.370
you can get either these
marbled cookie brownies

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:25.023
or these chocolate lava crunch cakes.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:29.820
They also throw in this, the sweet icing.

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:31.151
I'm sure it's amazing.

00:10:31.151 --> 00:10:34.848
So you can pour more
sugar all over the sugar.

00:10:35.740 --> 00:10:38.143
Let's put some icing on that lava guy.

00:10:39.094 --> 00:10:41.043
[laughs]

00:10:41.043 --> 00:10:43.010
Oh!

00:10:44.342 --> 00:10:46.760
That's too much. Stop!

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:49.150
I gotta get, I gotta, I'm gonna,
like, eat this whole tray.

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:50.500
I gotta get this out of my face.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:52.603
I'm ready to destroy these brownies.

